Subject: [PATCH 02692/11362] [outer-loop] Local CUDA validation:
 Qwen3.5-9B-MTP + MTP + q8 KV fits 16GB (11.5GB footprint), CUDA engine works

Ran the existing CUDA llama-server (CUDA 13, 3090, GPU idle, operator-directed one-off) with the exact
submission flags (--spec-type draft-mtp + q8_0 KV) on Qwen3.5-9B-MTP: MTP activated (80.5% accept),
generated correct code, 159 tok/s. VRAM footprint 11.5GB (model 5.9 + MTP self-draft ~5.2 + q8 KV @ 4096)
-> FITS a 16GB T4 with ~4.9GB free for KV. So the engine+model+MTP+KV+fit are validated on real CUDA.
Still Kaggle-only: the CUDA-VERSION-matched build (local links CUDA 13, Kaggle is ~12.x -> build-on-Kaggle
is mandatory, confirmed) + the live per-GPU VRAM probe -- exactly what the Kaggle notebook does.

